# Agent Workflows on Cursor

When the user asks to plan or run PR lanes, verify a branch, address review
comments, update a changelog, follow TDD, audit a merged batch, or monitor
coordinated agent work, read the matching Agent Workflows skill before acting.

Resolve the skill body in this order:

1. `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` when this host installed the pack
2. `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` or `~/.codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`
3. A repo-pinned `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`

Day-one and fleet names: `tdd`, `verify`, `address-review`, `update-changelog`,
`adversarial-pr-review`, `pr-batch`, `plan-pr-batch`, `close-batch`,
`post-merge-audit`, `batch-status`, `pr-monitoring`, `continue`,
`close-session`.

Do not substitute a different skill ecosystem for this process. Invoke with
`/<name>`. Cursor also loads Claude and Codex skill homes; prefer the
Cursor-installed copy when the same name exists in more than one home.

<!-- host-branch: cursor-only start -->
Pin the skill as a Custom Mode when you want it for the whole session.
Cursor Plan mode uses `SwitchMode` to `plan`. File-editing workers need their
own `git worktree add`; do not silently share the parent worktree. Overnight
multi-lane batches remain blocked on Cursor until worktree isolation is proven.
Never write into `~/.cursor/skills-cursor`.
<!-- host-branch: cursor-only end -->
